## Green cycle capture (2026-10-18 22:35:38 UTC)

A scheduler wait outlasted two short pauses during this handoff, and the
22:17 today backup rotated out the 22:17 yesterday set on schedule
(22:17:10 today → 22:17 yesterday reaches 24th position → evicted →
oldest now 23:17 yesterday). At 22:32:06 today, dg.service's retention
maintenance tick fired purge_expired and unlinked pet_*.sqlite files,
deleted their write_markers, and removed their databases rows. After
both events the digest names list collapses from 5 to 2 and every row
is durable-fresh.

Captured by `systemctl start dg-backup-digest.service` (no operator
flag-poking of the service; only the trigger) at 22:35:38 UTC; service
exited 0/SUCCESS and Result=success:

  Oct 18 22:35:38 micro2 systemd[1]: Starting dg-backup-digest.service ...
  Oct 18 22:35:38 micro2 dg[653113]: property                 | value
  Oct 18 22:35:38 micro2 dg[653113]: -------------------------+----------------------------------------------------
  Oct 18 22:35:38 micro2 dg[653113]: state                    | backup digest: 2 database(s) fresh
  Oct 18 22:35:38 micro2 dg[653113]: backup billing_dev_pilot | fresh @ 20261018T221710Z (1106s ago)
  Oct 18 22:35:38 micro2 dg[653113]: backup verify_probe      | fresh @ 20261018T221710Z (1106s ago)
  Oct 18 22:35:38 micro2 dg[653113]: action                   | no action; re-verify a set on demand with `dg backup verify`
  Oct 18 22:35:38 micro2 systemd[1]: dg-backup-digest.service: Deactivated successfully.
  Oct 18 22:35:38 micro2 systemd[1]: Finished dg-backup-digest.service - DB Gateway daily backup-health digest.

State counts: 2 fresh, 0 stale, 0 unknown. The bounded action contract
collapsed cleanly to "no action; re-verify a set on demand".

